# Anchored to the root on purpose. Unanchored, `Dockerfile` matches a file of
# that name at *any* depth, so adding one anywhere in the tree — a test fixture,
# for instance — silently never gets committed. The generated Dockerfile this
# line exists for is only ever at the root, written by `setup` from the
# fragments; the fragments themselves are `Dockerfile.frag` and were never
# matched.
/Dockerfile
start/target/
start/gen/schemas/
